n","title":"Count Down with JMU Classics","subtitle":"A senior milestone staged at EHall","notes":"Mark the fifty-day threshold with fellow graduates and the JMU-themed food and activities announced for that semester.","short_summary":"Graduating students pause at fifty days out for a JMU-specific countdown celebration.","evidence_claim":"The JMU Alumni Association lists 50 Days to Graduation as a tradition celebrated in both spring and fall with “JMU classics” at EHall.","source_url":"https://www.alumni.jmu.edu/s/1591/18/home.aspx?cc=1&gid=3&pgid=7813&sessionid=0be6db61-9c72-41fe-ab8f-90107366f6fb&sid=1591","source_title":"Madison Traditions","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"A spring-and-fall graduation countdown event; verify the semester’s date and participation details with the Alumni Association.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"jmu-duuuukes-response","subject_type":"tradition","entity_name":"J-M-U / Duuuuukes Cheer","title":"Answer J-M-U with Duuuuukes","subtitle":"A call, response and full-arm sweep","notes":"When someone calls “J-M-U,” answer “Duuuuukes,” step forward and sweep both arms outward to complete the response.","short_summary":"This JMU cheer pairs an elongated reply with a prescribed step-and-sweep motion.","evidence_claim":"JMU’s official game-day guidance directs fans to answer a shout of “J-M-U” with “Duuuuukes” while stepping forward, extending their arms and sweeping them outward.","source_url":"https://www.jmu.edu/student-life/spirit-traditions.shtml","source_title":"Student Life: Spirit and Traditions","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":"2025-12-10","source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Described by JMU as a typical game-day response; follow venue policies and event instructions.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"jmu-touchdown-streamers","subject_type":"tradition","entity_name":"Purple-and-Gold Touchdown Streamers","title":"Make Every Touchdown Rain Purple and Gold","subtitle":"JMU’s airborne score celebration","notes":"Bring only venue-permitted purple or gold streamers and toss them upward after a Dukes football touchdown.","short_summary":"Football scores trigger a burst of JMU-colored paper streamers from the stands.","evidence_claim":"JMU’s official spirit page tells fans to throw purple or gold streamers into the air when the football team scores a touchdown.","source_url":"https://www.jmu.edu/student-life/spirit-traditions.shtml","source_title":"Student Life: Spirit and Traditions","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":"2025-12-10","source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Associated with Dukes football games; admission and stadium policies depend on the event, so check current venue rules before bringing streamers.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"jmu-holding-doors","subject_type":"tradition","entity_name":"Holding Doors for Fellow Dukes","title":"Hold the Door Like a Duke","subtitle":"A small courtesy elevated into campus culture","notes":"Pause for the person behind you and hold the door; JMU presents the gesture as a daily expression of care and teamwork.","short_summary":"At JMU, an ordinary doorway courtesy is explicitly framed as a community tradition.","evidence_claim":"JMU’s official spirit-and-traditions page describes holding doors for others as “a way of life” on campus and connects the practice to caring and teamwork.","source_url":"https://www.jmu.edu/student-life/spirit-traditions.shtml","source_title":"Student Life: Spirit and Traditions","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":"2025-12-10","source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"acce